{"id": "sevt_01DRxE26q8m4LhXKnwUYuhaj", "content": [{"text": "Evidence lines up cleanly:\n\n- **Metric:** cart `p99_latency_ms` flat at ~75ms through 14:42, jumps to **3730ms at 14:43** and stays 3.5\u20134.6s after. `error_rate` stays ~0 \u2014 this is a latency problem, not errors.\n- **Deploy:** cart `df06e76` (\"price cart lines individually\", alice) at **14:43:20** is the only deploy that lines up. Checkout (14:41) and auth (14:44:50) don't.\n- **Diff:** the batched lookup `SkuPrice.objects.filter(sku_id__in=ids)` (one query, grouped in memory) was replaced by a per-line `SkuPrice.objects.filter(sku_id=line.sku_id)` inside a `for line in rows` loop \u2014 a classic N+1.\n- **Log confirmation:** the new per-row query `SELECT * FROM sku_prices WHERE sku_id = ?` first appears at **14:43:22.956Z** (zero occurrences before the deploy), ~820 queries after, fanning out to **16 queries per request** across 160 carts.\n\nThe fix is to revert to a single batched `sku_id__in` query (keep the readability refactor, drop the per-row DB call).\n\n> **Root cause:** `df06e76` \u2014 refactor replaced a single batched `sku_id__in` price lookup with a per-cart-line query, turning cart pricing into an N+1 that drove p99 from ~75ms to ~4s.", "type": "text"}], "processed_at": "2026-10-14T05:31:01.404708Z", "type": "agent.message"}
